meta {
  name: Shortlist Application Course
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/interviews/courses/{{applicationCourseId}}/shortlist
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "document_url": "https://cdn.example.com/offer-letters/OFR-ABC12345.pdf",
    "valid_until": "2026-09-15"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("offerLetterId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Marks an ApplicationCourse "shortlisted" and issues its OfferLetter in the
  same action — only allowed once its interview has been completed (status
  "interview_completed").

  Body (both required):
  - document_url: URL of the uploaded offer letter document (upload via
    college-admin's generic presign/verify flow first)
  - valid_until: ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) the offer expires on

  409 ConflictError "This course's interview hasn't been completed yet" if
  the course isn't at that stage. 409 ConflictError "Set a token amount for
  this course on the admission cycle before shortlisting" if
  AdmissionCycleCourse.tokenAmount isn't configured yet.

  tokenAmount on the created OfferLetter is copied from the admission
  cycle's configured AdmissionCycleCourse.tokenAmount. The document_url is
  only exposed to the student (via the application status endpoint) once
  the token payment status is "paid" — before that, the student can see the
  offer's amount/status but not download the letter.

  Re-calling this on an already-shortlisted course is a no-op that returns
  the existing OfferLetter (idempotent, does not re-issue).
}
